Modifications

hatterm is a modified version of Wave Terminal (https://github.com/wavetermdev/waveterm),
originally developed by Command Line Inc. and contributors.

Copyright 2026 Neil Manfred.

Summary of modifications:
- Rebranded user-facing names, window titles, app IDs, desktop entry, and package name
  from "Wave Terminal" / "waveterm" to "hatterm".
- Disabled telemetry by default; nulled out Wave cloud endpoints (api.waveterm.dev,
  ping.waveterm.dev) so no data is sent to Command Line Inc. servers.
- Disabled auto-update by default; update feed will point to hatterm's own releases.
- Renamed remote agent home directory from ~/.waveterm to ~/.hatterm.
- Renamed environment variables from WAVETERM_* to HATTERM_*.
- Extended AI provider layer (see docs/architecture-notes.md for details).
- Added drag-and-drop file copy between local host and remote sessions.
- Integrated native generative AI usage counter.

